---
title: What is a short answer?
term: Short answer
description: A short answer is a reply of forty to sixty words that opens a page and states its point, so a reader or a search engine can quote it alone.
publishDate: 2026-11-03
updatedDate: 2026-11-03
shortDefinition: A short answer is a reply of forty to sixty words at the top of a page. It states the whole point of the page, names its subject and makes sense without the text that follows it.
definition: |
  A short answer is the first paragraph a reader sees on a page. It answers the question the page exists for, in forty to sixty words, and it can be copied out of the page without losing its meaning. Search engines and answer engines quote such a paragraph, and readers use it to decide whether to read on.

  A short answer is not a summary of the page and not an introduction to it. A summary repeats the points in order, and an introduction announces what will come. A short answer gives the result first. It names the subject in full, so it stays clear when a search result shows it without the title.

  Every page of this site that answers a question carries one, and the author writes it last, after the rest of the page is final.
