## Why it comes up

A reader who lands on a page from a search result has a question and a few seconds. A page that opens with background makes that reader hunt for the result. A page that opens with a short answer gives the result at once, and the reader can then choose to read the detail or leave with what they came for.

## What to do about it

Write the page first, then write the short answer from the sentence that states the result. Keep it between forty and sixty words and name the subject in full. Read it alone, away from the page, and cut any word that points back at the page. The article on [how to write a short answer](/blog/how-to-write-a-short-answer) gives the steps.
